WEBVTT

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.453
Why has the battle with
Myath been suspended?!

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.621
It looks Glendan's drawing near.

00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:39.748
Glendan?!

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:43.126
Glendan's the Spear-Shelled City,
famous for its military arts.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:45.795
We're on standby so command
can quickly get ahold of us.

00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:49.841
If we go up against Glendan,
we won't stand a chance.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:54.054
They're the Spear-Shelled City,
but Zuellni's an academic city.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.056
No matter how much they want sernium,

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:58.683
they couldn't go against the treaty like that!

00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:02.854
Treaties don't mean shit.
If that's what the city wants,

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:04.731
then we humans can't stop it.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:08.318
Right now, we don't know <i>why</i>
Glendan's headin' toward Zuellni...

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:09.569
do we?

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.655
Layfon came from Glendan, did he not?

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:24.042
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:27.545
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:34.969
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.850
<i>Chizu o ushinatte samayotteiru machi</i>

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:44.312
<i>Owariyuku sekai demo</i>

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:51.027
<i>Karada no oku de hashiru</i>
<i>no o yamenai inochi o kikasete</i>

00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:54.322
<i>Tayasanai hikari o tozasanai hitomi ni</i>

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:57.575
<i>Kawaitemo yakitsuketa</i>

00:01:57.575 --> 00:02:04.332
<i>Kizutsuku koto mo naku</i>
<i>te ni suru mono nante nanimo shinjinai</i>

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:10.255
<i>Dareka ni mukatta hitosuji no omoi wa</i>

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:18.013
<i>Yoake no you ni hagane no yami o kirisaku</i>

00:02:18.013 --> 00:02:22.392
<i>Itsuka brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:26.021
<i>Dakara tsuyoku kaeru</i>

00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:32.068
<i>Kasaneta chikara mo inori mo</i>

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:35.739
<i>Kousa suru mirai, kakaeta negai</i>

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:39.159
<i>Dare no te ni mo watasenai</i>

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.702
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:45.707
<i>Kokoro o tsuraneru</i>

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:52.714
Glendan... Ominous, isn't it?

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:55.925
Whether our signal's
obstructed or just being ignored,

00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:57.802
they remain silent.

00:02:57.802 --> 00:03:01.514
If we fight Glendan,
we will have no hope of winning.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.976
Our one remaining
sernium mine will be taken from us.

00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:06.895
But is this even possible?

00:03:06.895 --> 00:03:10.273
An academic city battling a normal city...

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:14.527
Only the wills of the cities
themselves would know.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:18.031
<i>But right now, those wills...</i>

00:03:40.011 --> 00:03:42.681
Myath is increasing speed.

00:03:42.681 --> 00:03:45.266
It will be clear of the
battle zone in two hours.

00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:48.311
At present, there are no contaminoid readings.

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:52.315
Understood. Please continue your nen'i probe.

00:03:52.315 --> 00:03:55.777
Even after what she's been through,
you won't let Felli rest?

00:03:55.777 --> 00:03:59.030
She herself offered to help.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.950
Have the platoon members remain on standby.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.286
But the other military artists
should have some rest.

00:04:05.286 --> 00:04:06.913
Understood.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.792
Also, call the 17th Platoon to duty.

00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:13.670
Including Layfon?

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.421
Yes.

00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:16.089
Please wait.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:19.801
Layfon... was injured because of me.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:23.346
Also, Glendan is Layfon's home city.

00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:26.474
That is precisely why we require his help.

00:04:26.474 --> 00:04:31.354
Brother, do you know why I offered to help?

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:35.525
Please do not get Layfon
involved in this fight. I ask you.

00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:38.987
Vanzeh, I will contact Layfon myself.

00:04:40.655 --> 00:04:42.490
What is that?

00:04:45.744 --> 00:04:50.707
That aurora... I've seen it somewhere before.

00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:55.754
I know. I saw that same
sky long ago, near Glendan.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:59.799
"The Invincible, Spear-Shelled City
Glendan Draws Near!"

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:12.812
Thank goodness. Layfon...

00:05:14.731 --> 00:05:18.026
I'm sorry for not saying anything.

00:05:18.026 --> 00:05:21.404
Nina. I'm just glad you're all right.

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:24.032
You suddenly disappeared from Myath...

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:28.286
I'm sorry for making you worry.
It's just, I still don't understand

00:05:28.286 --> 00:05:31.331
what happened back then myself.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.667
But we were able to see each other again.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:36.878
Yes... How's Layfon?

00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:40.256
He's sleeping soundly. This way!

00:05:40.256 --> 00:05:42.634
No, I think I'll pass.

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:44.928
But you're already here.

00:05:44.928 --> 00:05:48.431
It won't make any difference
if all I do is see him sleeping.

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:51.518
I just wanted to know how he was doing.

00:05:51.518 --> 00:05:53.019
Oh...

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:55.021
Take good care of him.

00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:42.402
It wasn't a dream.

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:43.611
Layfon.

00:06:43.611 --> 00:06:47.365
It still hurts where you hit me.

00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:48.950
But I was so surprised.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.661
Leerin, you being here in Zuellni...

00:06:54.581 --> 00:06:58.335
They say you've been hospitalized
here several times already.

00:06:58.335 --> 00:07:00.754
The doctors told me.

00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:03.423
You left Glendan saying
you'd quit the military arts,

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.925
start all over.

00:07:07.135 --> 00:07:11.931
Was it for them? For Felli and Nina...

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:15.310
Are you sacrificing yourself again

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.771
for the sake of the people you fight alongside?

00:07:17.771 --> 00:07:19.606
That's not my intention at all.

00:07:19.606 --> 00:07:21.441
You lie!

00:07:22.484 --> 00:07:24.652
I spoke with Nina.

00:07:26.071 --> 00:07:27.781
Nina said...

00:07:27.781 --> 00:07:30.283
she couldn't forgive her own weakness,

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:32.202
for relying on a comrade.

00:07:32.202 --> 00:07:35.914
That "comrade" must be you, Layfon.

00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:42.295
I know full well how that feels.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:47.175
You always take on anything
and everything alone.

00:07:48.385 --> 00:07:51.096
Our leader said that?

00:07:51.096 --> 00:07:53.890
It's hard just being protected
all the time, you know.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:57.644
I always wanted you to rely on me more, too.

00:08:00.355 --> 00:08:04.526
I can't believe you had
that kind of talk with her.

00:08:04.526 --> 00:08:07.404
It was in Myath. She seemed to be all alone.

00:08:07.404 --> 00:08:08.738
In Myath?

00:08:08.738 --> 00:08:11.574
She was in Myath? What do you mean?

00:08:11.574 --> 00:08:12.492
Huh?

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:15.286
Uh, well...

00:08:15.286 --> 00:08:17.997
Please, tell me everything.

00:08:18.832 --> 00:08:20.959
Yeah. Okay.

00:08:44.733 --> 00:08:46.818
That's your hometown, Gor?

00:08:46.818 --> 00:08:48.194
Yeah, that's right.

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:50.030
We're gonna fight it next?!

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:53.366
I doubt it. There's no
precedent for an academic city

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:55.744
battling a regular city.

00:08:55.744 --> 00:08:59.080
I can't say it's absolutely impossible, though.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:03.209
If we <i>did </i>fight, whose side would you be on?

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:04.836
Who's that?!

00:09:08.465 --> 00:09:10.383
Yo.

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:11.343
Brother!

00:09:11.343 --> 00:09:12.844
What?!

00:09:16.681 --> 00:09:19.059
It's been a while, Gorneo.

00:09:19.059 --> 00:09:21.478
Brother, what are you doing here?

00:09:21.478 --> 00:09:23.563
An order from Her Majesty.

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:27.275
I finally arrived here by roaming bus,

00:09:27.275 --> 00:09:30.111
never suspecting that
Glendan was right behind me.

00:09:30.111 --> 00:09:34.366
So you don't know why Glendan
is approaching us, either?

00:09:34.366 --> 00:09:38.161
I assume it's the whimsy of Her Majesty,

00:09:38.161 --> 00:09:42.082
or else that even she is no
longer able to control Glendan's will.

00:09:43.333 --> 00:09:44.876
In any case...

00:09:44.876 --> 00:09:48.880
I will obey my order
and capture the Fallen Ones.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.007
Because it sounds like fun.

00:09:51.675 --> 00:09:55.762
Have you heard something
about the Fallen Ones?

00:09:55.762 --> 00:09:59.516
That a military artist named
Dinn was possessed by one.

00:09:59.516 --> 00:10:03.561
It was forcibly removed,
and now he's practically a vegetable.

00:10:03.561 --> 00:10:04.688
Huh.

00:10:04.688 --> 00:10:07.816
Also, while searching
the ruined city of Gandweria,

00:10:07.816 --> 00:10:12.404
Layfon said that he saw a golden goat.

00:10:12.404 --> 00:10:14.906
A golden goat?

00:10:14.906 --> 00:10:17.075
I didn't see it for myself.

00:10:19.494 --> 00:10:21.788
So even the Fallen Ones
can tell the commoners

00:10:21.788 --> 00:10:24.165
from those who are not.

00:10:24.165 --> 00:10:25.375
What's your problem?!

00:10:25.375 --> 00:10:28.586
I was looking forward to seeing Layfon again.

00:10:28.586 --> 00:10:30.714
I thought I could once again catch a glimpse

00:10:30.714 --> 00:10:34.217
of the strength he had in Glendan.

00:10:35.385 --> 00:10:37.137
Layfon fought his first battle
as a Heaven's Blade

00:10:37.137 --> 00:10:39.931
at an unprecedentedly young age.

00:10:41.141 --> 00:10:45.979
That battle was very... very fun.

00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:49.190
Battle is the only thing that uplifts me.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:52.110
No matter how skilled you are,
it takes only an instant to die.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:55.238
That is its own fun.

00:10:55.238 --> 00:10:58.366
I sensed some of that in Layfon.

00:10:58.366 --> 00:11:01.619
But just look at how idle he is now!

00:11:01.619 --> 00:11:05.498
Layfon, Layfon, Layfon!
All you're talking about is Layfon!

00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:09.419
Gorneo, this guy's a creep.
Is he really your brother?

00:11:09.419 --> 00:11:11.629
So because I'm the elder,
I should look more kindly

00:11:11.629 --> 00:11:13.715
on my mediocre younger brother?

00:11:14.257 --> 00:11:18.928
Still, you and Layfon
growing so close is a surprise.

00:11:18.928 --> 00:11:22.307
Gahard is probably rolling over in his grave.

00:11:23.141 --> 00:11:28.646
What, didn't you know?
Your brother disciple is dead.

00:11:28.646 --> 00:11:32.359
Gahard-<i>san</i>... is dead?

00:11:32.359 --> 00:11:33.777
Gor?

00:11:35.195 --> 00:11:35.945
You lie!

00:11:35.945 --> 00:11:40.325
It's true. I killed him with my own hands.

00:11:41.576 --> 00:11:46.706
He was a pitiful sight. His body
had been possessed by a contaminoid.

00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:49.167
Thinking of it still makes my skin crawl.

00:11:49.167 --> 00:11:50.794
It can't be!

00:11:51.461 --> 00:11:55.632
But thanks to him,
I could slay that contaminoid.

00:11:55.632 --> 00:12:00.887
Layfon had cut off his arm,
making him useless as a warrior,

00:12:00.887 --> 00:12:03.890
but in the end, Gahard still served Her Majesty.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:07.686
Hmm, I suppose in that
sense it was a noble death after all.

00:12:07.686 --> 00:12:12.023
You lie. You lie!

00:12:12.023 --> 00:12:14.943
Still, the little bit of consciousness that remained

00:12:14.943 --> 00:12:17.737
despised Layfon till the very end.

00:12:20.782 --> 00:12:22.200
Gor...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.418
Gor...

00:12:45.348 --> 00:12:49.144
Zuellni... Are you still inside me?

00:13:10.999 --> 00:13:13.543
This could take a turn for the worst...

00:13:13.543 --> 00:13:15.837
Vanzeh, Zuellni has changed course.

00:13:15.837 --> 00:13:17.589
We're directly facing Glendan.

00:13:17.589 --> 00:13:20.675
That's all we need. What should we do?

00:13:20.675 --> 00:13:23.470
They'll be right in firing range
of the kei-ra cannon.

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:25.055
Should we fire a shot at them?

00:13:25.055 --> 00:13:27.057
The kei-ra cannon, in an intermunicipal battle?

00:13:27.057 --> 00:13:30.060
I see. That could be an option.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.520
It was a joke. I take it back.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.398
That's a far bigger can of worms
than just "treaty violation."

00:13:35.398 --> 00:13:39.319
Get it ready. It will only be for intimidation.

00:13:39.319 --> 00:13:41.571
The Spear-Shelled City attacking us

00:13:41.571 --> 00:13:43.823
would itself violate the treaty.

00:13:48.745 --> 00:13:50.747
Layfon-<i>kun</i>, can you hear me?

00:13:50.747 --> 00:13:51.956
Yes, sir.

00:13:51.956 --> 00:13:53.833
Zuellni has begun to run amok.

00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:55.377
Run amok?

00:13:55.377 --> 00:13:58.380
Yes. It has turned toward
Glendan and is moving forward.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.506
Glendan?

00:13:59.506 --> 00:14:03.426
I feel like an idiot. After all
I went through on the roaming bus...

00:14:03.426 --> 00:14:06.012
That's what the shaking was before, wasn't it?

00:14:06.012 --> 00:14:09.307
It will probably not be long
before the two cities reach each other.

00:14:09.307 --> 00:14:12.310
But there has yet to be any
communication from Glendan.

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:14.979
And our platoon leader? Where is she?!

00:14:14.979 --> 00:14:17.482
The 17th Platoon has been called to duty.

00:14:17.482 --> 00:14:20.318
Understood. I'll be there soon.

00:14:21.945 --> 00:14:23.279
Don't go!

00:14:23.279 --> 00:14:24.406
Leerin...

00:14:24.406 --> 00:14:29.786
Her Majesty may have come
to welcome you back. Even if not...

00:14:29.786 --> 00:14:33.248
...if we make a request, she may grant it.

00:14:34.082 --> 00:14:37.252
I'm sure that she'd forgive you.

00:14:37.252 --> 00:14:40.547
So... let's go back together!

00:14:40.547 --> 00:14:42.173
Layfon!

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:53.226
Get the kei-ra cannon ready.

00:14:53.226 --> 00:14:54.644
Sir!

00:14:59.649 --> 00:15:01.484
Leerin, listen.

00:15:01.484 --> 00:15:04.362
You said I was being
sacrificed for other people,

00:15:04.362 --> 00:15:06.322
but that's not right.

00:15:06.322 --> 00:15:10.535
You and the others mean everything to me.

00:15:10.535 --> 00:15:14.039
That's why I thought, I have to protect you.

00:15:14.039 --> 00:15:17.208
Not because I had to,

00:15:17.208 --> 00:15:21.379
but because, truthfully, I <i>wanted </i>to.

00:15:23.131 --> 00:15:29.137
There may have been some
other way, if only I'd seen it...

00:15:31.139 --> 00:15:34.893
I'm sorry, Leerin. I'm going.

00:15:41.107 --> 00:15:42.525
Bye.

00:15:46.237 --> 00:15:48.031
Layfon...

00:15:48.031 --> 00:15:50.950
You'll come back, won't you?

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:04.422
I... What did I even come here for?

00:16:06.758 --> 00:16:08.134
Coming in, sir!

00:16:08.134 --> 00:16:11.888
We've been waiting for you.
Nina-<i>kun </i>is not yet here, though.

00:16:11.888 --> 00:16:14.516
There is something I have to report first.

00:16:14.516 --> 00:16:15.475
What would that be?

00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:20.605
Leerin came here by bus.
She says that on the way,

00:16:20.605 --> 00:16:22.816
she saw our leader in Myath.

00:16:25.026 --> 00:16:26.194
What does that mean?

00:16:26.194 --> 00:16:28.238
I asked for specifics, but unfortunately

00:16:28.238 --> 00:16:29.739
I couldn't make sense of it.

00:16:29.739 --> 00:16:33.284
But just before Nina disappeared from Myath,

00:16:33.284 --> 00:16:36.079
Leerin apparently saw the golden goat.

00:16:36.913 --> 00:16:38.707
That would explain Nina's disappearance

00:16:38.707 --> 00:16:43.753
and how she suddenly
reappeared in the middle of the desert.

00:16:48.425 --> 00:16:50.343
I wonder when it was...

00:16:50.343 --> 00:16:53.263
...that she was possessed by a Fallen One.

00:16:56.474 --> 00:16:58.727
If that's a joke, I ain't laughin'.

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:03.148
That's just not possible.

00:17:03.148 --> 00:17:06.317
So that is why at the same
moment that Nina returned,

00:17:06.317 --> 00:17:09.404
the dormant Zuellni began moving?

00:17:09.404 --> 00:17:11.865
Then why has Zuellni run amok?

00:17:11.865 --> 00:17:17.495
What do you think it means
that Zuellni is racing toward Glendan?

00:17:17.495 --> 00:17:19.039
I don't know.

00:17:19.039 --> 00:17:22.208
It's just a theory, but I'd like you to hear this.

00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:26.796
Both an electronic spirit and
a Fallen One reside inside Nina.

00:17:26.796 --> 00:17:29.257
At first the two achieved equilibrium,

00:17:29.257 --> 00:17:31.885
but for some reason that has been broken,

00:17:31.885 --> 00:17:36.306
and now Zuellni is more
deeply under the Fallen One's influence.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:44.606
Is forcibly removing the Fallen One
from Nina Antalk our only choice?

00:18:02.457 --> 00:18:04.459
If we can't do that...

00:18:13.343 --> 00:18:15.804
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:18:16.221 --> 00:18:18.223
Nina Antalk will...

00:18:27.273 --> 00:18:29.734
<i>What should I...?</i>

00:18:46.126 --> 00:18:49.004
Preparations are complete.
We can fire at any time.

00:18:49.004 --> 00:18:51.006
Huh? What is that?

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:05.770
What is it?

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:08.356
The sky... The aurora!

00:19:12.068 --> 00:19:13.903
What is that?!

00:19:22.662 --> 00:19:24.247
--A contaminoid!
--Impossible!

00:19:24.247 --> 00:19:26.332
From inside the aurora?!

00:19:26.332 --> 00:19:29.336
This is an emergency! Move to Level B!

00:19:31.546 --> 00:19:33.840
You are hereby authorized to fire

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.009
the kei-ra cannon on the contaminoid!

00:19:36.009 --> 00:19:38.970
You... Don't tell me you knew!

00:19:40.597 --> 00:19:43.683
Emergency alert. We are at Threat Level B.

00:19:43.683 --> 00:19:48.438
All civilians, please head
for the shelters at once. I repeat.

00:19:48.438 --> 00:19:52.734
Emergency alert.
We are at Threat Level B. I repeat.

00:19:52.734 --> 00:19:55.695
Emergency alert. We are at Threat Level B.

00:19:55.695 --> 00:19:58.156
All civilians, please head
for the shelters at once.

00:19:58.156 --> 00:20:00.700
Please take shelter this way!

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.828
No pushing! We foresee
possible secondary disasters!

00:20:03.828 --> 00:20:06.831
Please make your escape calmly.

00:20:06.831 --> 00:20:10.585
Why would Glendan attack?
There's no reason for it!

00:20:10.585 --> 00:20:13.338
You there, are you all right?

00:20:13.338 --> 00:20:14.964
Thank you.

00:20:25.558 --> 00:20:27.435
Dainsleif.

00:20:34.651 --> 00:20:37.946
Your Majesty, what is that contaminoid?

00:20:37.946 --> 00:20:40.824
The youngster for which I have longed.

00:20:41.825 --> 00:20:43.535
In any case...

00:20:43.535 --> 00:20:48.456
For it to appear when Leerin
had gone over to Zuellni...

00:20:48.456 --> 00:20:51.459
It's too much to be coincidence, perhaps?

00:20:52.919 --> 00:20:56.047
Saya, just what are you after?

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:18.862
The escape elevators in the
leg section are active. Confirm.

00:21:18.862 --> 00:21:21.364
Confirmed. There is one occupant.

00:21:21.364 --> 00:21:24.075
I'll verify the occupant's name.

00:21:24.701 --> 00:21:31.082
Verified. It's Nina Antalk. Nina Antalk,
leader of the 17th Platoon.

00:21:36.254 --> 00:21:38.298
You, huh?

00:21:38.298 --> 00:21:41.009
Where do you think you're taking me?

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:46.097
The kei-ra cannon is ready to fire.

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.392
Beginning countdown.

00:21:49.392 --> 00:21:54.105
Ten, nine, eight, seven...

00:21:54.105 --> 00:21:57.776
six, five, four...

00:21:57.776 --> 00:22:00.028
three, two...

00:22:00.028 --> 00:22:01.488
one.

00:22:01.488 --> 00:22:03.114
Fire!

00:22:26.262 --> 00:22:36.356
<i>Haikei, anata wa dare o omotteimasu ka</i>

00:22:36.356 --> 00:22:43.446
<i>Kono tegami wa mada mune no naka</i>

00:22:43.446 --> 00:22:53.498
<i>Totsuzen fureta anata no kioku no kakera</i>

00:22:53.498 --> 00:23:00.588
<i>Kokoro ni sasatte, ugokenai</i>

00:23:00.588 --> 00:23:05.427
<i>Kizuite hoshii, kizukanaide</i>

00:23:05.427 --> 00:23:09.139
<i>Tsumetaku suru no wa koi no sei? </i>

00:23:09.139 --> 00:23:18.732
<i>Tsutaetai yo, soba ni ite yo, demo ienai</i>

00:23:19.524 --> 00:23:28.116
<i>Yogoreta kono sekai de anata ni deaeta yo</i>

00:23:28.116 --> 00:23:39.294
<i>Watashi no kokoro ni maiorita</i>
<i>kiseki kanadete kudasai</i>

00:23:39.294 --> 00:23:47.135
<i>Ai no Zuellni</i>

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:55.894
<i>A contaminoid larger than any</i>
<i>before it has emerged from an aurora</i>

00:23:55.894 --> 00:23:57.145
<i>that engulfed the sky.</i>

00:23:57.145 --> 00:23:59.522
<i>Nina, upon learning</i>
<i>that the Fallen One inside her</i>

00:23:59.522 --> 00:24:01.024
<i>is the reason for Zuellni's running amok,</i>

00:24:01.024 --> 00:24:04.527
<i>leaves the city to face the contaminoid alone.</i>

00:24:04.527 --> 00:24:06.529
<i>Next time, "Ignacius's Fragments," and...</i>

00:24:06.529 --> 00:24:08.171
<i>Restoration!</i>
